// The Canberra river system.
// The root rivers are googong, jerrabombarra and upper_molongolo.
// googong flows into dam1 and then into queanbeyan.
// central_molongolo is queanbeyan, upper_molongolo and jerrabombarra joined together,
// and it flows through dam2 into lower_molongolo which is the output of the whole system.
//
// dam1 and dam2 are used here like they've already been declared, and they're connected with <-.
// The grammar already supports <- so this file parses fine. See the grammar in the README.
// It only fails when it runs, with an "undefined river or dam" runtime error.
// That's because there is no dam { ... } declaration yet, so dam1 and dam2 never actually exist.
// Adding dam declarations and making <- actually work when it runs is the next step.
var googong = flow[10ML @ 1 ~ 2];
var jerrabombarra = flow[4ML @ 1 ~ 1];
var upper_molongolo = flow[6ML @ 2 ~ 3];

print("Root rivers declared OK. Attempting dam1 connection next (expected to fail -- see comment above):");

var queanbeyan = dam1 <- googong;
var central_molongolo = queanbeyan + upper_molongolo + jerrabombarra;
var lower_molongolo = dam2 <- central_molongolo;

print(lower_molongolo);
